From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: add the RPM master stats

The RPM keeps one sleep record per master in its message RAM: how often
and when the APSS, the modem, the ADSP, the CDSP and TZ shut down, and
how often and for how long each let XO go. They name the master that
keeps the SoC out of XO shutdown, which the SoC-wide vlow and vmin
counts of qcom_stats cannot.

The offsets are the vendor node's (bengal-pm.dtsi
qcom,rpm-master-stats@45f0150: five masters, 0x1000 apart), and the
stock MANGMI Air X device tree has the same node. Each slice is the 0x50
bytes of one record (struct rpm_master_stats); the APSS one ends below
the MPM block at 0x1b8. The node sits under the RPM processor, where the
binding and mainline's MSM8226 and MSM8974 put it.

Read on the MANGMI Air X, 7.3.5, with the same offsets given in the
board file: all five records, the APSS shutdown and XO shutdown counts
rising by one per suspend.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi
@@ -372,6 +372,20 @@
 	rpm: remoteproc {
 		compatible = "qcom,sm6115-rpm-proc", "qcom,rpm-proc";
 
+		master-stats {
+			compatible = "qcom,rpm-master-stats";
+			qcom,rpm-msg-ram = <&apss_master_stats>,
+					   <&mpss_master_stats>,
+					   <&adsp_master_stats>,
+					   <&cdsp_master_stats>,
+					   <&tz_master_stats>;
+			qcom,master-names = "APSS",
+					    "MPSS",
+					    "ADSP",
+					    "CDSP",
+					    "TZ";
+		};
+
 		glink-edge {
 			compatible = "qcom,glink-rpm";
 
@@ -1098,8 +1112,28 @@
 			#size-cells = <1>;
 			ranges = <0 0x0 0x045f0000 0x7000>;
 
+			apss_master_stats: sram@150 {
+				reg = <0x150 0x50>;
+			};
+
 			apss_mpm: sram@1b8 {
 				reg = <0x1b8 0x48>;
+			};
+
+			mpss_master_stats: sram@1150 {
+				reg = <0x1150 0x50>;
+			};
+
+			adsp_master_stats: sram@2150 {
+				reg = <0x2150 0x50>;
+			};
+
+			cdsp_master_stats: sram@3150 {
+				reg = <0x3150 0x50>;
+			};
+
+			tz_master_stats: sram@4150 {
+				reg = <0x4150 0x50>;
 			};
 		};
 
